From d024dfd326a86e2fae8e62c44189c22f99a83233 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 17:42:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 24/26] software_isp: Gather focus statistics over a window the
 IPA sets

The sharpness for contrast autofocus is gathered over the centre half
of the statistics window, so an application can't focus on what the
user taps. Let the IPA move that window through a new focusWindow in
the debayer parameters (x, y, width and height in fractions of the
statistics window, the centre half by default), and gather a luminance
histogram over the same window for spot metering.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
